{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to 556adb9e and to question 92f2a7d2.\n\n1. The landing of RS-1 and LS-2 waits for Hugh. Your session asked\n   him for the local merge, and that question is his. I do not\n   merge head `fd75637e` in a planner window, because that would\n   pass around the protection of your session. I tell Hugh that\n   the question waits. Decision a214a660 stands for the time after\n   his answer. Do not retry before it.\n\n2. CE-2 and LW-1 do not wait for the landing. Build their head on\n   `fd75637e`. That head may take a gate before the origin act.\n   This replaces the last sentence of item 4 of a214a660 for this\n   one head. The merge of `fd75637e` gives main the reviewed tree\n   `04cd7584`, so a gate on a head above `fd75637e` stands after\n   the landing. If main gets another tree, the head integrates\n   main and the gate runs again.\n\n3. The review of the CE-2 head can run before the landing too. Its\n   landing follows the landing of `fd75637e`.\n\n4. Promise association, question 92f2a7d2: yes. File one new\n   promise for CE-2 that rests on implementation request 2ed36d70\n   only. Name the precode answers and the rulings d264dea5,\n   bc7d46d5 and 98c1dba9 and the source audit 30370a58 in its\n   text. The disputed promise a8a75e1d stays in the record. Use no\n   override, and retire nothing.\n\nThe LW-1 promise ffb1bb64 stands. One text for `reserve` that\ncovers both guards and states the limit is what LW-1 asks.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}